             <property name="maximumSize">
              <size>
               <width>16777215</width>
               <height>19</height>
              </size>
             </property>
             <property name="toolTip">
              <string>How a set that carries an opacity source is built.&#10;Auto: as Transparent when the set has a usable opacity source.&#10;Transparent: alpha blend. Only for a material that covers just the translucent surfaces &#8212; a solid body wearing it renders through the transparent queue (no depth write) and shows its own back faces, in the DCC and in every engine.&#10;Masked: alpha cutout. The opacity map is the mask (Maya&#8217;s Stingray PBS: TEX_mask_map, red channel, cut at mask_threshold, which Unity imports as Autodesk Interactive Masked; Blender: the Principled BSDF&#8217;s alpha, clipped); opaque queue, safe on solid bodies, cheapest in VR.&#10;None: opacity ignored. A standalone opacity map is dropped and a colour map&#8217;s alpha is left unwired, so the solid shader is built even when the set could make it transparent.</string>
             </property>
             <property name="editable">
              <bool>false</bool>
             </property>
             <property name="maxVisibleItems">
